      "name": "DispatchCallbackIfValid",
      "signature": "uint DispatchCallbackIfValid(void * pData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Dispatches a callback function if a valid function pointer is stored in a global variable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the callback function pointer from global variable at 0x6fa2b228\n2. Check if the pointer is null using TEST EAX, EAX\n3. If null, jump to return with default value\n4. If valid, prepare parameters: load data from pData at offset +4 and +1\n5. Call the callback function pointer indirectly\n6. Return 1 to indicate callback was processed\n\nParameters:\n- pData: Implicit parameter in ECX, pointer to data structure passed to callback\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Always returns 1 (success/true), indicates callback dispatch completed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 1 even if function pointer is null (no error differentiation)\n- Uses implicit calling convention with parameter in ECX register\n- Loads 16-bit value at offset +1 and 32-bit address at offset +4 from pData\n- The actual function called depends on contents of global 0x6fa2b228",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
