      "name": "AppendStringToBuffer",
      "signature": "char * AppendStringToBuffer(char * pSourceString, int * pSizeTracker, int nMaxSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Appends a source string to a tracking buffer with size validation.\nCalculates the length of the source string, verifies the total size\ndoes not exceed the maximum limit, and copies the string to the\ndestination buffer. Used extensively in encoding operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate source string length by iterating until null terminator\n2. Load current size tracker value from memory location\n3. Calculate new total size (current + source length + 1 for null)\n4. Compare new total size against maximum allowed size (nMaxSize)\n5. If size exceeds limit, call error handlers and abort\n6. Copy source string character-by-character to destination buffer\n7. Null-terminate the destination buffer\n8. Return pointer to the appended string data\n\nParameters:\n- pSourceString (ECX): Pointer to null-terminated source string\n- pSizeTracker (EDX): Pointer to size counter variable (updated in-place)\n- nMaxSize (Stack+0x4): Maximum buffer size limit for validation\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Pointer to the beginning of appended string in destination buffer\n  or no return on buffer overflow (calls error handlers instead)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty source string: Still updates size tracker by 1 (null terminator)\n- Size overflow: Calls GetReturnAddress and CleanupAndAbort error handlers\n- Destination pointer (EDI): Passed implicitly as implicit __fastcall parameter",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
