      "name": "DispatchCallbackByIndex",
      "signature": "int DispatchCallbackByIndex(byte * pIndexPointer, int bEnabled)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Dispatches to one of 26 callback functions from a table based on a byte index.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Initialize return value to 0\\n2. Check if bEnabled flag is set (EDX > 0)\\n3. If not enabled, return 0 immediately\\n4. Load index byte from *pIndexPointer\\n5. Validate index is less than 0x1a (26)\\n6. If invalid, return 0\\n7. Look up function pointer from callback table at [0x6fa2a900 + index*4]\\n8. If pointer is non-null, call it and return result\\n9. If pointer is null, return 0\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pIndexPointer (ECX): Pointer to byte containing index into callback table\\n- bEnabled (EDX): Enable flag; if 0 returns 0 immediately\\n\\nReturns:\\n- EAX: Result from called callback, or 0 if disabled, index invalid, or callback is null\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Index must be < 0x1a (26 valid indices)\\n- Returns 0 for disabled, invalid index, or null callback pointers\\n- Callback table at 0x6fa2a900 contains 26 function pointers\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nCallback Table at 0x6fa2a900:\\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Description\\n0x00   | 4    | callback[0]   | Function pointer for index 0\\n0x04   | 4    | callback[1]   | Function pointer for index 1\\n...\\n0x64   | 4    | callback[25]  | Function pointer for index 25\\nTotal: 104 bytes (26 entries \\u00d7 4 bytes)",
