      "name": "ValidateAndDispatchCallback",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndDispatchCallback(void * pData, uint nSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates input size and dispatches to registered callback function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare input size (nSize) against minimum threshold of 2 bytes\n2. If size is less than 2, return 0 (invalid)\n3. Load callback function pointer from global data location 0x6fa2b234\n4. If callback pointer is null, skip invocation and return 1\n5. Extract offset value from input data at [pData + 0x1]\n6. Calculate dispatch address by adding offset to data pointer (pData + 0x2)\n7. Invoke callback with dispatch address and adjusted size parameter\n8. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n- pData (ECX): Pointer to input data structure containing metadata and payload\n- nSize (EDX): Total size of input data in bytes (must be >= 2)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 if nSize < 2 (validation failed)\n- 1 if nSize >= 2 and callback handling completed (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Callback may be null; in this case function skips invocation\n- Input size 2 is the minimum valid threshold\n- Callback receives adjusted parameters derived from input offset\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n-------|------|-------|------|-------------\n0x0    | 1    | ?     | byte | Unknown/unused byte\n0x1    | 1    | offset| byte | Offset value for callback dispatch\n0x2+   | nVar | data  | ?    | Callback payload data",
