      "name": "ProcessDataPacket",
      "signature": "uint ProcessDataPacket(byte * pPacket, uint packetSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Process a binary data packet and update global buffer state.\n\nThis function processes incoming data packets by validating their structure,\ncopying data into a global buffer, and invoking registered callback handlers\nfor packet processing. It maintains a global buffer and state tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate packet size is at least 8 bytes (minimum header)\n2. Extract packet fields: byte at offset 1, width at offset 4, height at offset 2/6\n3. Check if all dimension fields are zero - if so, reset global state and callbacks\n4. Validate height field is at least 0xc (12 bytes)\n5. Update global buffer size if height differs from current\n6. Calculate total required size: width + height\n7. Verify global buffer has capacity for required data\n8. Copy packet data into global buffer using dword then byte copies\n9. Update global position counter\n10. If buffer capacity reached, invoke optional pre-processing callback\n11. Loop through processing items: extract count and height from buffer\n12. Validate item parameters: count < 0x100, height < 0x10, calculated size valid\n13. For each valid item block, invoke packet handler callback with dimensions\n14. Decrement position and continue until buffer exhausted\n15. Reset buffer position to zero on completion\n16. Return 1 on success, 0 on validation failure\n\nParameters:\n  pPacket (ECX): Pointer to binary packet data with header and payload\n  packetSize (EDX): Size of packet data in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  uint: 1 if packet processed successfully, 0 if validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Packet size < 8 returns immediate failure\n  - All zero dimensions trigger state reset with callback invocation\n  - Height < 0xc returns failure (minimum size requirement)\n  - Insufficient buffer space returns failure\n  - Callback pointers may be null; operations skipped if null\n\nGlobals Used:\n  DAT_6fa2b240: Global data buffer (destination for packet payload)\n  DAT_6fa2b238: Current buffer position/size tracker\n  DAT_6fa2b23c: Current offset within buffer\n  DAT_6fa2b22c: Optional packet handler callback pointer\n  DAT_6fa2b230: Optional pre-processing callback pointer\n  DAT_6fa2b22c: Handler function receives (height, byte, buffer_ptr)",
