      "name": "InitializeBufferConfig",
      "signature": "void InitializeBufferConfig(void * pConfigStruct)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes buffer configuration from a config structure with conditional data processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract configuration fields from pConfigStruct at offsets: +0x1, +0x5, +0x9, +0xd\n2. Store extracted fields to global variables (DAT_6fa2aed8, DAT_6fa2aeb0, DAT_6fa2b1c8)\n3. Test if offset +0x9 (processing flag) is non-zero\n4. If processing flag set: call CopyInetNtoaToBuffer(0x12), then DecodeDataBuffer with destination/source\n5. Set initialization flag DAT_6fa2aeac = 1\n6. If offset +0xd (config value) is zero: set it to default value 0x28\n7. Return\n\nParameters:\n- pConfigStruct: Pointer to configuration structure with data fields at specific offsets\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If offset +0x9 is non-zero, data processing functions are invoked\n- Offset +0xd defaults to 0x28 if initially zero\n- Always sets initialization completion flag DAT_6fa2aeac to 1\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n+0x1    4     field1      DWORD   First config field\n+0x5    4     field2      DWORD   Second config field  \n+0x9    4     procFlag    DWORD   Processing flag (triggers DecodeDataBuffer if non-zero)\n+0xd    4     configVal   DWORD   Config value (defaults to 0x28)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
