      "name": "LoadGameStatePacket",
      "signature": "int LoadGameStatePacket(void * pPacket)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Loads and processes a game state packet into global memory buffers.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load packet header fields (magic, value, mode byte) and validate magic match\\n2. Return error 0x32 if value is -1 (invalid state)\\n3. Return error 0x33 if value is -2 (forbidden state)\\n4. Copy name string from packet (+0x2F) to global buffer at 0x6fa2b05c\\n5. If mode byte is non-zero, process array of mode records:\\n   - For each record, copy 2-byte header and array element data\\n   - Write to alternating global arrays at 0x6fa2b09c and 0x6fa2b0bc\\n   - Repeat for count specified in mode byte field\\n6. Return 1 (success)\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pPacket (void*): Pointer to game state packet structure with offsets:\\n    +0x1: magic word validation value\\n    +0x3: dword state value (-1 and -2 are errors)\\n    +0x7: dword configuration value\\n    +0xB-0xD: 3 config bytes\\n    +0xE: byte array count/mode flag\\n    +0x1F-0x2E: mode record data array\\n    +0x2F: null-terminated name string\\n\\nReturns:\\n  int: Always returns 1 on success\\n  Side effects: Sets error code in global 0x6fa2b1c8 for invalid packets\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  Magic validation at offset +0x1 fails if not 0x6fa2aeb4\\n  Values -1 and -2 trigger early return with error codes\\n  Empty mode byte (zero) skips array processing loop\\n  String copy uses strlen-style null-termination detection",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
