      "name": "ValidateAndInitializeRecord",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndInitializeRecord(int * pRecord)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates a record against a global type value and conditionally initializes global state with record data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global type identifier from DAT_6fa2aeb4\n2. Compare word at pRecord+1 with the loaded type value\n3. If types match:\n   - Copy dword at pRecord+7 to DAT_6fa2b1c8\n   - Copy dword at pRecord+3 to DAT_6fa2aed8\n   - Store type value in DAT_6fa2aea8\n4. Return 1 (success code)\n\nParameters:\npRecord (int*): Pointer to record structure with at least:\n  Offset +1: Word containing record type identifier\n  Offset +3: Dword configuration/state value 1\n  Offset +7: Dword configuration/state value 2\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If record type does not match global type, globals are not modified\n- Function always returns 1 regardless of validation result\n- Accesses global DAT_6fa2aeb4 as type identifier source",
