      "name": "InvokeCallbackIfSet",
      "signature": "int InvokeCallbackIfSet(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Conditionally invokes a callback function if one is registered.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load callback function pointer from global state (0x6fa2b224)\n2. Check if callback pointer is null\n3. If null, skip to return\n4. If not null, prepare parameters from ECX register:\n   - Load word from [ECX + 0x1] into CX (parameter)\n   - Load address [ECX + 0x3] into EDX (pointer parameter)\n5. Call the callback function via EAX\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- ECX (implicit): Pointer to context structure with fields at +0x1 and +0x3\n\nReturns:\n- EAX = 1 (always returns true/success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If callback pointer at 0x6fa2b224 is null, function skips execution and returns 1\n- Function does not validate ECX pointer before access\n- Callback may modify game state during execution",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:3d4e3339d7bcb6ead5f6fd1c93d47c1f",
