      "name": "ProcessNetworkDataPacket",
      "signature": "uint ProcessNetworkDataPacket(byte * pPacketData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Processes incoming network data packets with validation and decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load packet signature from bytes +0x1 and compare against expected signature\n2. If signature mismatch, jump to error return (invalid packet header)\n3. Extract and cache packet metadata: signature word, timestamp (offset +0x3), buffer address (offset +0xb)\n4. Load optional size field from offset +0x7\n5. If size is zero, check custom size field at offset +0xf\n6. If custom size exists, store it; otherwise use default size of 0x28 bytes\n7. If size was non-zero at offset +0x7, proceed to decode phase\n8. Call CopyInetNtoaToBuffer(0x12) to process network address\n9. Call DecodeDataBuffer to decode packet payload with buffer and size\n10. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pPacketData: Pointer to network packet structure with header and payload fields\n              Contains signature (word at +0x1), optional size fields, and data references\n\nReturns:\n  Returns 1 on success (packet processed or validation complete)\n  Implicit side effects: Updates global state variables with packet metadata\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Invalid signature immediately returns success code (0x6fa26531)\n  - Size field of 0x28 bytes is used as default when optional size is absent\n  - Custom size at offset +0xf takes precedence over default\n  - Decode operations only occur when size field at +0x7 is non-zero\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Packet Header Format (accessed via pPacketData):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name       Type         Description\n  -----------------------------------------------\n  +0x0    1     reserved         byte         Padding/reserved\n  +0x1    2     signature        word         Packet type identifier\n  +0x3    4     timestamp        dword        Packet timestamp or ID\n  +0x7    4     dataSize         dword        Size of packet data\n  +0xb    4     bufferAddress    dword        Address of data buffer\n  +0xf    4     customSize       dword        Optional custom size override",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:57262212d47b665deee328cd256f2143",
