      "name": "CopyStringsToMemory",
      "signature": "dword CopyStringsToMemory(dword pDestStr1, dword pDestStr2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Copies two null-terminated strings to specified memory locations and returns global data pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load source address 0x6fa2b1c0 into pcVar2\n2. Calculate destination offset: pDestStr1 - 0x6fa2b1c0\n3. Loop: copy bytes from source to destination until null terminator (0x00)\n4. Load second source address 0x6fa2ae88 into pcVar2\n5. Calculate destination offset: pDestStr2 - 0x6fa2ae88\n6. Loop: copy bytes from source to destination until null terminator (0x00)\n7. Return value from DAT_6fa2ae80 (global data pointer)\n\nParameters:\n- pDestStr1 (dword): Destination address for first string copy\n- pDestStr2 (dword): Destination address for second string copy\n\nReturns:\n- dword: Pointer value from global data location 0x6fa2ae80\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses relative addressing with pre-calculated source base addresses\n- Copies strings in-place with memory offset adjustment\n- Both strings are null-terminated; copy loop includes null terminator",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
