      "name": "GetPeerAddress",
      "signature": "void GetPeerAddress(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves the peer socket address from a global socket structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve socket handle from field at offset 0x110 of the global socket data\n2. Check if socket handle is valid (non-zero)\n3. If valid, initialize a 0x10-byte buffer with size marker\n4. Call GetPeerSocketAddress to populate the buffer\n5. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global socket data at DAT_6fa2b028\n\nReturns:\nvoid - populates internal buffer via GetPeerSocketAddress side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if socket handle is zero (no active socket)\n- Buffer size field is hardcoded to 0x10 bytes",
