      "name": "InitializeWorkerThread",
      "signature": "void InitializeWorkerThread(void * pConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes a worker thread for processing game configuration data (singleton pattern).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if worker thread has already been created by testing handle at DAT_6fa2b1d0\n2. If thread exists (handle != NULL), skip initialization and return\n3. If thread not created, copy 82 DWORDs (328 bytes) from input configuration buffer to global data area at DAT_6fa2aee0\n4. Create worker thread using CreateThread with entry point at FUN_6fa26ba0 and NULL context\n5. Store returned thread handle in DAT_6fa2b1d0 for future checks\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npConfig (void *): Pointer to 328-byte configuration data structure containing worker thread parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function has no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Singleton initialization: Function may be called multiple times but only creates thread once\n- Thread handle storage: DAT_6fa2b1d0 serves as guard to prevent duplicate thread creation\n- Configuration copy size: 82 DWORDs (0x52 in decimal) must match source buffer size exactly\n- Thread entry function: FUN_6fa26ba0 is the worker thread's main procedure",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
