      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes buffer encoding operation with default parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 8 bytes of local stack space for encoding parameters\n2. Clear global state variable at 0x6fa2b1c8 to 0\n3. Initialize encoding mode parameter to 0x19 (25 decimal)\n4. Initialize buffer size parameter to 0x8 (8 decimal)\n5. Call EncodeBufferWithContext with global buffer pointer, parameter block, and mode constant 5\n\nParameters:\nNone - Parameterless initialization function\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe hard-coded values 0x19 and 0x8 represent fixed encoding parameters passed to the encoder. The constant 5 represents the encoding operation mode or parameter count.",
