      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the encoding context and buffer for data encoding operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the encoding state flag at global address 0x6fa2b1c8 (set to 0)\n2. Allocate a local buffer on the stack for encoding work\n3. Load the global context pointer from 0x6fa2b028\n4. Call EncodeBufferWithContext with:\n   - First parameter: Global context pointer (from 0x6fa2b028)\n   - Second parameter: Address of local encoding buffer\n   - Third parameter: Mode/type flag (0x1)\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - returns control to caller after initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention with callee-side stack cleanup\n- The magic value 0x1 passed to EncodeBufferWithContext indicates initialization mode\n- The local buffer is referenced via [ESP+7] during execution\n- Global state at 0x6fa2b1c8 is the encoding state flag\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe function operates on two global data structures:\n- Address 0x6fa2b028: Context pointer (used as first parameter)\n- Address 0x6fa2b1c8: Encoding state flag (cleared during initialization)",
