      "comment": "Initializes the buffer encoder and prepares it for encoding operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ECX register on stack to preserve caller state\n2. Load encoder context pointer from global 0x6fa2b028\n3. Clear encoder status flag at 0x6fa2b1c8 (set to 0)\n4. Allocate local buffer on stack (1 byte)\n5. Set buffer magic byte to 0x0f at ESP+0xf\n6. Call EncodeBufferWithContext with context pointer and buffer\n7. Restore ECX from stack and return\n\nParameters:\nNone. Uses global encoder context at 0x6fa2b028.\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value 0x0f written to buffer indicates initialization marker\n- Global flag at 0x6fa2b1c8 is cleared before encoding starts\n- Uses __stdcall convention with callee cleanup\n\nStructure Layout:\nLocal stack structure (8 bytes):\n[ESP+0x0]  4 bytes  Saved ECX register\n[ESP+0x4]  1 byte   Encode buffer (encodeBuffer)\n[ESP+0x5]  3 bytes  Padding\n[ESP+0x8]  1 byte   Encode mode parameter (value 1)\n[ESP+0xf]  1 byte   Magic marker (value 0x0f)",
