      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Processes input data and encodes it using a context pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global flag at 0x6fa2b1c8 to 0\n2. Initialize local buffer (1024 bytes) with first byte = 0xc (marker)\n3. Call FUN_6fa26ec0 to process pInputData into the buffer\n4. Validate processed size does not exceed 0xfffe (65534)\n5. If validation fails, call GetReturnAddress and CleanupAndAbort with error code 0x1de\n6. On success, call EncodeBufferWithContext to encode the processed buffer\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pInputData (ECX, char*): Input data pointer (filename or buffer to process)\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function does not return a value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer size validation uses <= 0xfffe to prevent overflow\n- Global flag at 0x6fa2b1c8 is used to track processing state\n- DAT_6fa2b028 is the encoding context pointer\n- Error handling calls abort function (does not return)\n\nStructure Layout:\n- Local stack buffer: 1028 bytes (1KB + 4 bytes)\n- First byte (offset 0): Magic marker 0xc\n- Remaining 1027 bytes: Processed data\n- Byte offset 0x408: Additional stack space allocation",
